7	## The Problem: Protocol Violations
8	
9	Hardware protocols have **strict state machines**. An IPMI session has states:
10	Unauthenticated → Authenticated → Active → Closed. PCIe link training goes through
11	Detect → Polling → Configuration → L0. Sending a command in the wrong state
12	corrupts the session or hangs the bus.
13	
14	**IPMI session state machine:**
15	
16	```mermaid
17	stateDiagram-v2
18	    [*] --> Idle
19	    Idle --> Authenticated : authenticate(user, pass)
20	    Authenticated --> Active : activate_session()
21	    Active --> Active : send_command(cmd)
22	    Active --> Closed : close()
23	    Closed --> [*]
24	
25	    note right of Active : send_command() only exists here
26	    note right of Idle : send_command() → compile error
27	```
28	
29	**PCIe Link Training State Machine (LTSSM):**
30	
31	```mermaid
32	stateDiagram-v2
33	    [*] --> Detect
34	    Detect --> Polling : receiver detected
35	    Polling --> Configuration : bit lock + symbol lock
36	    Configuration --> L0 : link number + lane assigned
37	    L0 --> L0 : send_tlp() / receive_tlp()
38	    L0 --> Recovery : error threshold
39	    Recovery --> L0 : retrained
40	    Recovery --> Detect : retraining failed
41	
42	    note right of L0 : TLP transmit only in L0
43	```
