65	## Type-State Pattern
66	
67	With type-state, each protocol state is a **distinct type**. Transitions are methods
68	that consume one state and return another. The compiler prevents calling methods in
69	the wrong state because **those methods don't exist on that type**.
70	
71	```rust,ignore
72	use std::marker::PhantomData;
73	
74	// States — zero-sized marker types
75	pub struct Idle;
76	## Case Study: IPMI Session Lifecycle
77	
78	pub struct Authenticated;
79	pub struct Active;
80	pub struct Closed;
